# DARKVEDA LAB — iptables base rules (reference only, do NOT iptables-restore directly).
# Plain `iptables-restore` FLUSHES Docker's DOCKER chains and breaks bridged
# containers (db/ipam DNAT error). netstack/entrypoint.sh sets OPEN policies
# (INPUT/FORWARD/OUTPUT ACCEPT, no DROP rules) via `iptables -P` + cleanup.
# Keep the two in sync.
# Firewall is OPEN by design: no blocking, no per-interface 445/139 rules.
*filter
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:FORWARD ACCEPT [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
# No -A rules: all traffic allowed (Docker chains managed by Docker itself).
COMMIT
*nat
:PREROUTING ACCEPT [0:0]
:INPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:OUTPUT ACCEPT [0:0]
:POSTROUTING ACCEPT [0:0]
# Examples (uncomment as needed):
# Road-warrior client via WireGuard (replace .3 with the client /32):
#-A POSTROUTING -s 10.99.0.3/32 -o eth0 -j MASQUERADE
#-A POSTROUTING -s 10.99.0.3/32 -d 172.16.0.0/24 -o wg0 -j MASQUERADE
#-A POSTROUTING -s 10.99.0.3/32 -d 192.168.10.0/24 -o wg0 -j MASQUERADE
COMMIT
